# .cursorrules — Arellan Hnos Core Ecosystem

## Project
ERP System for Arellan Hnos Automotive Clinic, Lima, Peru.
Family business with an automotive workshop. See arellan-docs-governance for complete context.

## Stack
- Backend: NestJS + TypeScript + Prisma + PostgreSQL + Redis
- Frontend admin: Next.js 14 App Router + Tailwind + Zustand
- Mobile: Next.js PWA + next-pwa
- Mechanic UI: React + Vite (optimized for touch tablets)
- Client portal: Next.js with SSR and SEO

## Coding Conventions
- Code language: English (variables, functions, classes)
- Comment language: Spanish (the team is Spanish-speaking)
- NestJS: one module per business domain (vehicles, finance, employees, etc.)
- File names: kebab-case for files, PascalCase for classes
- DTOs always validated with class-validator
- Never use `any` in TypeScript
- Always handle errors with try/catch blocks and standard ApiResponse<T> responses

## Security (critical)
- All endpoints protected with @UseGuards(JwtAuthGuard, RolesGuard)
- Finance module: minimum test coverage 85%
- Never log financial information or personal data
- Inputs are always sanitized before reaching the database

## Business Context
- The siblings (Edgar, Juan, Ana) are the only ones with the OWNER role
- The mechanics only have access to vehicles and inventory
- The daughter has the FINANCE role with access to finance and reports
- All cash outflows require approval from at least one sibling
- Registered vehicles belong to customers, never to the workshop

## Strict Coding Standards
- **Naming Conventions:** Everything must be generic (e.g., `WorkshopCore`, `MechanicController`, `CashboxRegistry`). NEVER hardcode client names like "Arellan Hnos" or developer names into code or namespaces.
- **Security Principle of Least Privilege:** Every endpoint must explicitly enforce an authorization guard (e.g., `@Roles(Role.Owner, Role.Finance)`).
- **Anti-Fraud Audit Trail:** Any mutation operation (CREATE, UPDATE, DELETE) on financial or inventory records MUST trigger an immutable log entry through the `AuditLogService`.

## Git Mandates (Plan B - Discipline-Enforced)
- Direct pushes to `main` are strictly prohibited by code of honor.
- Every feature must be developed in `feature/*` and merged into `develop` via a Pull Request reviewed by the partner developer.